+# Part-settle an OPEN claim: split the body's amount off it exactly as split does, then settle the new claim at once
+# by the user exactly as settle does (PENDING when the clerk limit says so). The settle's four-eyes and proof rules are
+# judged on the original claim, before anything is written (the new claim's opener is the user, who may still settle it).
+# A split or a settle that would be refused refuses the whole action (400) and writes nothing. Responds with the new claim.
